paragraphs:
People say they know many things;
But look! those things have taken wings—
The arts and sciences,
And a thousand useful devices;
The wind that blows
Is all that anyone knows.

“Grief consumes the sorrowful before their time;
Their days are few in the land of the living,
Beautiful daughter of Toscar.”

Light-winged Smoke, Icarian bird,
Melting your pinions in your upward flight,
Lark without song, and messenger of dawn,
Circling above the hamlets as your nest;
Or else, departing dream, and shadowy form
Of midnight vision, gathering up your skirts;
By night star-veiling, and by day
Darkening the light and blotting out the sun;
Go, my incense, upward from this hearth,
And ask the gods to pardon this clear flame.
